  "stillBetterFit": {
    "heading": "When Tiller Is Still the Better Fit",
    "body": "Tiller remains the closer match for users who want complete ownership over their financial data inside Google Sheets or Microsoft Excel. Unlike closed applications that store transactions inside proprietary databases, Tiller automatically delivers daily bank transactions and balances into spreadsheets you control. This allows you to build custom pivot tables, create multi-year net worth models, and calculate specialized formulas without software constraints.\n\nTiller also avoids recurring month-to-month subscription traps by offering a clear, predictable fee of $99 per year, equivalent to $8.25 per month. Tiller states that its service includes no advertisements and no hidden fees. New users receive a 30-day free trial where payment cards are not charged until the trial ends, followed by a 30-day full refund window. That provides up to 60 days of risk-free evaluation. You sign up simply with an existing Google or Microsoft account, keeping authentication straightforward."
  },
  "verdict": "Tiller delivers automated bank sync into private Google Sheets and Microsoft Excel files for $99 per year, while alternatives offer dedicated mobile and web applications with varied pricing structures. Monarch Core lists at $99.99 per year, YNAB costs $109 per year with sharing for up to six people, Copilot Money offers a single plan at $109 per year, EveryDollar Premium costs $79.99 per year alongside a $0 manual tier, and Simplifi offers cloud tracking with forward cash projections. To choose the right Tiller alternative, write down whether you require spreadsheet flexibility or an app interface, check the supported devices, and compare the annual costs in our table.",
